1

ORDINANCE NO. _____________

ENTITLED: “AN ORDINANCE AMENDING SECTION 5.12.100, TEMPORARY
PERMITS, OF CHAPTER 5.12, ALCOHOLIC LIQUOR AND MALT
BEVERAGES, OF TITLE 5, BUSINESS LICENSES AND REGULATIONS,
OF THE MUNICIPAL CODE OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING.”

BE IT ORDAINED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE,
WYOMING:

Section 1.  That Section 12.100, Temporary permits, of Chapter 5.12, Alcoholic Liquor and
Malt Beverages, of Title 5, Business Licenses and Regulations, is hereby amended as set out in this
ordinance.  Sections currently existing in Chapter 5.12 not set out within this ordinance remain
unchanged.

12.100 Temporary permits.

D.   The chief of police, or authorized designee, may revoke temporarily suspend for
no longer than four (4) hours any temporary permit issued under this chapter to maintain
peace and order; health, safety and welfare of the public; for situations in which an
emergency arises, or where there is an immediate threat to the security, property and welfare
of any member of the public.  The chief of police, or authorized designee, will work with the
permittee to regain order; health, safety and welfare of the public and reinstate the permit at
the earliest opportunity, if it can be done safely.  The chief of police will submit a report to
the governing body within twenty-four (24) hours of the suspension of the permit outlining
the specific reasons for the emergency suspension.  Only the governing body has the
authority to revoke a temporary permit.  The governing body shall hold an emergency
hearing if requested by the chief of police or city clerk to revoke any temporary permit. The
governing body shall convene and consider the revocation request within twenty-four (24)
hours of the request for revocation.  If the permit has expired, the hearing may be held during
a regularly scheduled meeting.  The governing body shall receive testimony from city
officials and the holder of the temporary permit and reach a conclusion on the request to
revoke the temporary permit by a majority vote of the governing body within twenty-four
(24) hours of the hearing.

Section 2.  This ordinance shall become effective upon its passage and publication.

FIRST READING:______________________________________________________________

SECOND READING:___________________________________________________________

THIRD AND FINAL READING:__________________________________________________

_________________________________________
Marian J. Orr, Mayor
(SEAL)

ATTEST:

___________________________________
Kristina F. Jones, City Clerk
By Michael O'Donnell at 8:59 am, May 04, 2020
